shieldmap: licence notice

1. src/shieldmap/ingest/xsec.py

The evaluation path in this file (main program, labels 220-600, and the subroutines SCOF/BSPOL/BLIN) is a
line-by-line port of XCOM.f, the program distributed with the NIST XCOM photon cross-section database (NIST
Standard Reference Database 8). The header of XCOM.f states: "Copyright 1999, Martin J. Berger. Permission is
given to use the program for non-commercial purposes." To the extent that it derives from XCOM.f, xsec.py is
excluded from the MIT grant in LICENSE and carries the same non-commercial condition. Everything else in src/,
scripts/, tests/, paper/*.py and docs/figures/*.py is under the MIT licence.

2. Upstream data

No raw upstream file is redistributed. The NIST XCOM package, the NIST SRD 126 tables, the Materials Project
snapshot, the Crystallography Open Database archive, the ENSDF distribution, the ENDF/B-VIII.0 library and the
IAEA TRS-457 report are fetched from their providers and verified by SHA-256 (scripts/fetch_raw.py,
config/sources/*.yaml). The NIST SRD 126 air table and test fixtures, and the per-element crustal abundances
(CRC Handbook via mendeleev), are restored by scripts/restore_nist_srd126.py and
scripts/restore_crustal_abundance.py. ICSD collection codes are not distributed; only the Materials Project's
ICSD-match flag and the number of ICSD codes it lists per entry appear.

3. Derived tables

Compound-level tables derived from these sources are distributed under CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-data) with the
attribution in README.md. NIST is the source of the photon cross sections and air energy-absorption
coefficients from which the compound-level values were computed.

